2026-09-27T12:05:55.7580670Z Description:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7581604Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7582031Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7583043Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7584175Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7584281Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7584516Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7584875Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7585218Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7585324Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7585574Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7585737Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7585922Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7586373Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7586643Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7586776Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7587109Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7587320Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7587487Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7587953Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7588390Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7589223Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7589887Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7589995Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7590466Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7591045Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7592304Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7592821Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7593391Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7593618Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7593817Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7593942Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7595364Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7596889Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7597128Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7597644Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7598477Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7599131Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7599747Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7600180Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7600611Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7667986Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7668520Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7668789Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7669882Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7671068Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7671867Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7672748Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:55.7672969Z 
